{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'for f in design-decision.md source-freeze.json preimages.json handover.md handover.json parent-source-verification.json; do echo \"FILE $f\"; cat \".flow/artifacts/fn-109-gomad-deepen-modules-and-tool-interfaces/task-8/$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"FILE design-decision.md\nTask 8 completes R4 by adding capability inspection to internal/preparation and migrating analysis and compatibility review. Use an owned inspection handle with an explicit Close: compatibility authoring reads the prepared Spec and rewritten module/overlay inputs after the capability review, so the workspace must survive until those consumers finish. Keep the public analysis wrapper API and existing private CLI injection behavior usable; avoid public inaccessible types or aliases to the internal owner. Let the new owner select adapters, own the private root, obtain mode-appropriate review evidence, and carry adapter identities. Durable campaign and portable roots stay untouched.\n\nClosure review lists and evaluates without build or launch; linked review may compile without launching. Keep guarded policy and error identities through wrapping. Preserve fixed-input text/JSON and authoring outputs on successful cleanup. Cleanup failures must be returned/surfaced; test the meaningful error path, including primary-error preservation. CLI error distinctions between adapter preparation and capability review remain. Architecture edges expand only for consumers actually migrated. Host-command and installation extraction belong to tasks 9/10, capability decomposition to task 11, native Linux qualification to task 21.\nFILE source-freeze.json\n{\n  \"frozen_at\": \"2026-10-03T14:25:47.590388+00:00\",\n  \"sources\": {\n    \"tools/gomad3/architecture_test.go\": \"0a73d30b0ddf8e0d8e40e096320a29c722bd4c1985bf195753c946006aba8470\",\n    \"tools/gomad3/cmd/gomad/internal/cli/analyze.go\": \"c55ac32805ccda0b0a0