ea5cbaa39db1a1d8615afad343f8dac49b48bdc176e63\",\n  \"tools/gomad3/qualification/analysis/prepared_review_test.go\": \"b3ca39aabc7e409a3fb6be4e6afbbfb8619610ea37015c5822b13570ce25a3ce\",\n  \"tools/gomad3/cmd/gomad/internal/cli/analyze.go\": \"cb4f0c9892968176b6768a0e9c370ee3add229c694def4fc6fe1bff202330bc2\",\n  \"tools/gomad3/cmd/gomad/internal/cli/cli_test.go\": \"0797fb0f755db4fcd3b47d1bf29868f3d967f93adca080b87963f306545c6d8c\",\n  \"tools/gomad3/cmd/gomadtool/compatibility_pack.go\": \"b2386dfb0a2c98787dd30e86bafe31aa3e0e5dffbc56a89671e53700a6d59de6\",\n  \"tools/gomad3/architecture_test.go\": \"c02a298b6060dfdde7a77df85d83b3db0c6d112b26fbd5860e27d22658cfd176\"\n}\nFILE handover.md\n# Task 8 source handoff\n\nFrozen at `2026-10-03T14:25:47.590388+00:00`. The seven task-owned Go source hashes in `source-freeze.json` were rechecked after all gates. `preimages.json` binds byte-for-byte originals captured before edits; `task-only.patch` is the original-to-final task diff, with `task-only-lint.patch` using module-relative paths for the linter. `handover.json` references each captured command receipt, which retains argv, environment, exit, duration, and raw stdout/stderr hashes.\n\n`internal/preparation.Inspect` owns a private capability-inspection workspace, adapter selection, review evidence, adapter identities, and explicit `Close`. CLI analysis consumes the owner review directly and returns status 3 if cleanup fails after success. The public `qualification/analysis.PrepareCapabilityReview` API delegates ownership and `Close` to the same operation. The owner preserves adapter and capability error identity and separates adapter/review stages for CLI error precedence.\n\nThe pre-edit CLI binary and current CLI produced byte-identical text and JSON for the fixed supported fixture. Real unsupported closure, invalid adapter sum, and invalid package fixtures retained byte-identical outputs and statuses 1, 2, and 2. A pre-edit gomadtool binary was rebuilt with `old-gomadtool-overlay.json` mapping the captured original source bytes; its compatibility-pack qualify output matches the current binary byte-for-byte. `snapshots.json` records all comparisons. No normalization was required; the private workspace path is absent from these outputs.\n\nTests prove closure inspection passes a Go shim that rejects target builds and a target that would panic if launched; linked inspection emits a manifest without writing its target-launch sentinel. A malformed linked build record remains a review-stage infrastructure error. Adapter sums, unsupported closure `errors.As`, caller root rejection, and cleanup failures retain their distinctions. The supported-report cleanup regression first failed with status 0 in `red-cli-cleanup` and passed after the change. The initial unsupported test expectation used the finding label rather than the established `UnsupportedCapabilityError.Capability` text; `focused-classification` retains that test-only failure and `focused-classification-fixed` passed.\n\nFrozen gates: `final-quick` exit 0, `final-architecture` exit 0, `final-compatibility` exit 0, `final-vet` exit 0, and `final-task-lint` exit 0. The single full Darwin host gate ran `GOFLAGS='-tags=test_dep -count=1' make -C tools/gomad3 test-host` from the repository root: exit 0, 180.885 seconds, 46 packages passed, empty stderr. `make runner` rebuilt `.bin/gomad` (SHA-256 `16da20e81277ec7214d1ea007ef45cee0664eede7ac9ac46b265de46c5cf36e6`), and its supported JSON smoke output matches the pre-edit bytes. The pinned build key is `2ecdbd330bb5928f360739fdd80cb3eb0f0764e513a5cc208cd83714fff0a457`.\n\nNative Linux qualification remains task 21 work and was not run on this Darwin host. No git or Flow lifecycle operation was performed by the source writer.\nFILE handover.json\n{\n  \"frozen_at\": \"2026-10-03T14:25:47.590388+00:00\",\n  \"verified_at\": \"2026-10-03T14:30:57.002073+00:00\",\n  \"source_sha256\": {\n    \"tools/gomad3/architecture_test.go\": \"0a73d