{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A55 -B5 '\"'^## Acceptance Criteria|'\"\\\\*\\\\*R4:\\\\*\\\\*' .flow/specs/fn-109-gomad-deepen-modules-and-tool-interfaces.md\"","aggregated_output":"208-  worktrees, leave commits to the user and retain native/default behavior.\n209-- At ten times campaign work, keep policy state bounded by declared frontier,\n210-  parallelism, retention and evidence limits. Avoid total-selection-sized state\n211-  or extra complete-payload copies introduced solely by extraction.\n212-\n213:## Acceptance Criteria\n214-\n215-- **R1:** Local and isolated campaigns use one normalized options owner.\n216-  `MaxForcedDecisions`, `MaxExplorationResultBytes` and every\n217-  `SimulationDimensionLimits` field survive coordinator transport. Tests\n218-  exercise seed, choice and simulation strategies through actual isolated\n219-  execution with distinguishable nonzero limits. Errors: invalid/missing bounds,\n220-  incompatible strategy settings, malformed requests and unknown fields remain\n221-  rejected; local fake-executor tests alone do not fulfill transport coverage.\n222-  [paraphrase]\n223-- **R2:** Seed, choice and simulation completion use fn-108's shared private\n224-  computational assessment. Fixed-input projections and classifications match\n225-  the pre-extraction behavior. Errors: malformed/missing World evidence, wrong\n226-  seed, coverage/choice errors, watchdog, cancellation and simultaneous faults\n227-  preserve precedence and strategy-specific effects. Fulfilled through fn-108\n228-  R6 with linked evidence. [paraphrase]\n229-- **R3:** Shared retention and artifact composition hide novelty, capacities\n230-  and payload assembly while preserving seed, round and corpus transactions.\n231-  Errors: duplicate failures, incomplete transcripts, count/byte exhaustion,\n232-  publication failure, cancelled/interrupted commits and failed corpus replay\n233-  preserve bounded evidence and committed policy state. Fulfilled through\n234-  fn-108 R7 with linked evidence. [paraphrase]\n235:- **R4:** Explore, portable planning, analysis and compatibility review use one\n236-  complete preparation owner returning validated target/review evidence with\n237-  adapter identities attached. Workspace cleanup is owned explicitly. Tests\n238-  cover fresh/cache builds, external modules/local replacements, custom\n239-  preparers and independent qualification preparations. Errors: invalid sums,\n240-  replacement conflicts, unsupported closure, malformed linked records,\n241-  changed binaries and cleanup failures retain classifications. Closure\n242-  inspection does not compile or execute. [paraphrase]\n243-- **R5:** Public executor injection moves behind private dependencies, with all\n244-  repository consumers migrated and supported external use compiled from\n245-  outside the Runner subtree. Keep usable preparation/replay seams and fake\n246-  failure coverage through private adapters. Errors: inaccessible internal\n247-  types, global mutable test hooks and exposed descriptor mechanics fail\n248-  acceptance; execution failures retain existing semantics. Fulfills D3.\n249-  [paraphrase]\n250-- **R6:** CLI operation construction resolves installation/private modes once\n251-  and shares semantic normalization with Runner. Plan and explore share parsing\n252-  directly. Tests cover documented command grammar, explicit zero/irrelevant\n253-  flags, environment/tags/argv, text/JSON output and exit statuses. Errors:\n254-  malformed input and output-writer failures retain existing behavior; a\n255-  changed default or hidden plan-only argument route fails acceptance.\n256-  [paraphrase]\n257-- **R7:** Simulation-time layout and codecs have one generated definition with\n258-  host and runtime-safe consumers. Cross-consumer vectors preserve bytes and\n259-  exercise actual runtime consumption on both platforms. Errors: truncated\n260-  frames, wrong magic/kind, nonzero reserved bytes, generation mismatch and\n261-  time regression fail as before. Generated-output drift fails validation.\n262-  [paraphrase]\n263-- **R8:** Architecture checks discover every host package on both qualified\n264-  source sets and enforce targeted ownership, host-effect and public-signature\n265-  visibility rules. Negative fixtures demonstrate rejection of an ownerless\n266-  new root, forbidden effect/import edge and inaccessible public type. Valid\n267-  platform files and explicit overlay/fixture exclusions remain accepted.\n268-  Errors: silently uninspected packages and checks based only on filename\n269-  presence fail acceptance. Fulfills D4. [paraphrase]\n270-- **R9:** Current architectural guidance describes both supported platforms,\n271-  implemented choice replay/exploration and both backends, using existing\n272-  requirement IDs. Separate capability support, repeatability, exact replay\n273-  and expectation matching. Document current residual findings and intentional\n274-  Go interface changes. Errors: unmeasured support or performance claims,\n275-  obsolete delivery-state claims and failures described as qualification\n276-  success fail acceptance. Fulfills D5. [paraphrase]\n277-- **R10:** Target compilation, Go identity queries and listing use a coherent\n278-  private host-command seam with contextual lifetime and output limits. Tests\n279-  cover command cancellation/termination, long diagnostics and cache-lock\n280-  release. Errors: structured-output overflow, malformed listing, unsupported\n281-  capability, timeout and cleanup failure stay distinct; truncated structured\n282-  data cannot be accepted. [paraphrase]\n283-- **R11:** Compare at least two simulation-progress interfaces and implement\n284-  the chosen lifecycle owner, removing caller-owned multi-counter sequencing\n285-  and duplicate response-barrier bookkeeping. Tests cover forwarding,\n286-  acknowledged arrivals, delivered-but-unconsumed work, arrival at quiescence,\n287-  cancellation with late committed response, death and restart. Errors:\n288-  unknown acknowledgement, abandoned response and stale incarnation fail\n289-  before invalid progress or model mutation; concurrent blocking operations\n290-  remain possible. Design evidence alone leaves this requirement unmet.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
